sequenceDiagram
  actor C as Cliente
  participant Ch as SPA/App + BFF
  participant AP as API Management
  participant TS as Transfer Service
  participant Core as Core ledger
  participant Rail as Red interbancaria
  participant DB as PostgreSQL + Outbox
  participant SB as Service Bus
  participant N as Notification Service
  C->>Ch: Orden + step-up + Idempotency-Key
  Ch->>AP: HTTPS, access token, request hash
  AP->>TS: JWT audience/scope validado; correlationId
  TS->>TS: Revalidar titularidad, límites y riesgo
  TS->>DB: RECEIVED + clave idempotente
  alt Transferencia propia
    TS->>Core: Comando idempotente
    Core-->>TS: POSTED o rechazo final
  else Transferencia interbancaria
    TS->>Core: Reservar/debitar según contrato
    TS->>Rail: Solicitar pago con referencia externa
    Rail-->>TS: Aceptado, rechazado o pendiente
    Note over TS,Rail: Timeout conserva PENDING; consultar estado, no repetir ciegamente
  end
  TS->>DB: Estado + Outbox en misma transacción
  DB-->>TS: Commit
  TS-->>Ch: Referencia + estado explícito
  DB->>SB: Relay Outbox; entrega al menos una vez
  SB->>N: Evento versionado TransactionPosted
  N->>N: Deduplicar eventId; guardar bandeja y preferencias
  N-->>C: Push y Email/SMS según política
